    "prompt": "In the diagram, ABCDE is a regular pentagon. DEF is an equilateral triangle. The size of angle AEF (the angle marked, measured on the side of $D$) is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2001-r2/q05.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$168^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$150^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$120^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$132^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$170^\\circ$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Add the angles",
        "body": "Each interior angle of a regular pentagon is $\\frac{(5-2)\\times180^\\circ}{5}=108^\\circ$, so $\\angle AED=108^\\circ$. Triangle $DEF$ is equilateral, so $\\angle DEF=60^\\circ$.\n\nThe marked angle $AEF$ passes through $ED$, so it equals $108^\\circ+60^\\circ=168^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (A) $168^\\circ$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
