    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In the weekly Lotto six different numbers are drawn randomly from the numbers $1,2,3,\\dots,49$. Mpho's parents bought a ticket with the numbers $2;17;26;29;30;43$ on it. The first five numbers drawn were $17;26;30;2$ and $43$. What is the chance that the next number drawn will be $29$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$\\frac12$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac16$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac1{30}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac1{44}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac1{49}$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Remaining numbers",
        "body": "Five of the $49$ numbers have been drawn, leaving $44$ equally likely numbers. Exactly one of them is $29$, so the chance is $\\frac1{44}$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $\\frac1{44}$**"
      }
    ],
