    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Observe: $1.5\\times1.5=2.25$, $2.5\\times2.5=6.25$, $3.5\\times3.5=12.25$. The value of $\\square$ if $\\square\\times\\square=9900.25$ is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$33.5$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$66.5$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$99.5$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$100.5$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$300.5$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the pattern",
        "body": "The pattern is $(n+0.5)^2=n(n+1)+0.25$: e.g. $3.5^2=12.25=3\\times4+0.25$. So we need $n(n+1)=9900$. Since $99\\times100=9900$, $n=99$ and $\\square=99.5$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 99.5**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "patterns",
      "algebra"
    ],
