    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The entrance fee at a concert was R5 per child and R16 per adult. A total of R789 was raised. The maximum number of people who could have attended the concert was",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$37$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$38$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$138$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$149$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$157$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Divisibility",
        "body": "Let there be $a$ adults and $c$ children: $16a+5c=789$. Modulo $5$: $16a\\equiv a$ and $789\\equiv4$, so $a\\equiv4\\pmod 5$: $a=4,9,14,\\dots$.\n\nTo maximise $a+c$ we want as many cheap tickets as possible, i.e. the fewest adults: $a=4$, $c=(789-64)/5=145$. (Replacing $5$ adults by $16$ children keeps the total the same in rand but changes the head count by $+11$, so more children and fewer adults means more people; hence we take the smallest possible $a$.)\n\nTotal: $4+145=149$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 149**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory",
      "money"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null,
    "wrongPoints": -1
