    "prompt": "ABCD is a rectangle such that $AD=2AB$. If $AC=\\sqrt5\\,d$, then the perimeter of ABCD is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$4\\sqrt5\\,d$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$6\\sqrt5\\,d$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$10d$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$6d$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$8d$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pythagoras",
        "body": "Let $AB=x$, so $AD=2x$. Then $AC^2=x^2+4x^2=5x^2=5d^2$, so $x=d$.\n\nPerimeter $=2(x+2x)=6x=6d$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $6d$**"
      }
    ],
