      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count all, remove isosceles",
        "body": "Sides $a\\le b\\le c$ with $a+b+c=23$ and $c\\le11$ (triangle inequality):\n\n- $c=11$: $(1,11),(2,10),(3,9),(4,8),(5,7),(6,6)$ — 6\n- $c=10$: $(3,10),(4,9),(5,8),(6,7)$ — 4\n- $c=9$: $(5,9),(6,8),(7,7)$ — 3\n- $c=8$: $(7,8)$ — 1\n\nThat is $14$ triangles. The isosceles ones are $(1,11,11)$, $(3,10,10)$, $(5,9,9)$, $(7,8,8)$, $(7,7,9)$, $(6,6,11)$: $6$ of them (no equilateral since $3\\nmid23$).\n\n$14-6=8$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 8**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
