        "title": "Compound growth",
        "body": "Each week the weight is multiplied by $1.2$: $1.2^2=1.44$, $1.2^3=1.728$, $1.2^4=2.0736$.\n\nThe weight first exceeds double after $4$ weeks. (If the $20\\%$ were simple, non-compounding growth it would take $5$ weeks; the paper's key uses compounding.)\n\n**Answer: (B) 4**"
      }
