    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count the meetings",
        "body": "In the time Johnny runs $1$ lap, Sarah runs $3$ laps in the opposite direction, so together they cover $4$ laps and meet $4$ times (including the finishing meeting at the start). So Johnny collects R4 per lap he runs, i.e. R4 for every $3$ laps of Sarah.\n\nFor R120 he needs $30$ laps, so Sarah runs $30\\times3=90$ laps.\n\n**Answer: (E) 90**"
