    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Place values",
        "body": "If the number $N$ has $k$ digits then putting a $2$ at both ends gives $2\\cdot10^{k+1}+10N+2$. The increase is $2\\cdot10^{k+1}+9N+2=2317$. The increase $2317$ is between $2000$ and $20000$, so $10^{k+1}=1000$, i.e. $k=2$: then $2000+9N+2=2317$, so $9N=315$ and $N=35$.\n\nDigit sum: $3+5=8$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 8**"
