      {
        "title": "Arcs of a circle",
        "body": "Each roll is a rotation of the block through $120^\\circ$ about a vertex of the triangle, so $P$ moves along an arc of a circle of radius $PC=2$ (the distance from the centre to a vertex) through $120^\\circ$: length $\\frac13\\cdot2\\pi\\cdot2=\\frac{4\\pi}3$.\n\nThe diagram shows $6$ rolls (seven positions of the triangle), so the path has length $6\\times\\frac{4\\pi}3=8\\pi$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $8\\pi$**"
