        "key": "C",
        "text": "$213$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$287$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$284$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Residues mod 7",
        "body": "Sort the numbers by remainder on division by $7$. Since $500=71\\times7+3$, remainders $1,2,3$ occur $72$ times each and remainders $0,4,5,6$ occur $71$ times each.\n\nTwo numbers have a sum divisible by $7$ exactly when their remainders add to $7$ (pairs $1\\&6$, $2\\&5$, $3\\&4$) or both have remainder $0$. So from each pair of remainder classes we may keep only one class: choose the bigger one ($72$ each, i.e. remainders $1,2,3$), giving $3\\times72=216$. From remainder $0$ we may keep at most one number.\n\nMaximum: $216+1=217$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 217**"
      }
    ],
